<title>USA: Caterpillar unit files shelf for $800 mln.</title>
<headline>Caterpillar unit files shelf for $800 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Caterpillar Financial Funding Corp filed a shelf offering Wednesday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for up to $800 million in asset-backed securities.</p>
<p>When combined with a previous registration, the Las Vegas-based company's offering totals $854 million, according to the SEC filing.</p>
<p>The certificates represent an interest in a pool of sales contracts and leases on new and used machinery made by Caterpillar Inc.</p>
</text>
